 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 9359,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Logic programming allows expressing medical rules as logical clauses, and the inference engine derives diagnoses using backtracking and pattern matching without procedural control flow.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>A medical diagnosis system needs to infer conditions based on symptoms. How is logic programming beneficial in such a scenario?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 106,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9359
  },
  {
   "_id": 9360,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Regulations can be encoded as facts and rules, allowing logical evaluation and automated reasoning to validate whether constraints are met.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>A legal compliance system must verify adherence to numerous regulations. Why is logic programming appropriate for this purpose?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 106,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9360
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 9386,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Logic programming is suitable for rule-based systems as it allows defining relationships and rules declaratively. Prolog can be used to express medical knowledge:</p>\n\n<p>symptom(john, fever).<br />\nsymptom(john, rash).<br />\ndiagnosis(Patient, measles) :- symptom(Patient, fever), symptom(Patient, rash).</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3716\" data-start=\"3499\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3556\" data-start=\"3499\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3556\" data-start=\"3501\">In this example, <code data-end=\"3524\" data-start=\"3518\">john</code> has symptoms of fever and rash.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3640\" data-start=\"3557\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3640\" data-start=\"3559\">The rule defines that if a patient has both symptoms, the diagnosis is <code data-end=\"3639\" data-start=\"3630\">measles</code>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3716\" data-start=\"3641\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3716\" data-start=\"3643\">When queried as <code data-end=\"3685\" data-start=\"3659\">diagnosis(john, Disease)</code>, the system returns <code data-end=\"3715\" data-start=\"3706\">measles</code>.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"3827\" data-start=\"3718\">This paradigm emphasizes <strong data-end=\"3774\" data-start=\"3743\">declarative rule definition</strong>, <strong data-end=\"3799\" data-start=\"3776\">automatic inference</strong>, and <strong data-end=\"3826\" data-start=\"3805\">logical deduction</strong>.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Develop a rule-based medical diagnosis system using logic programming. Justify the choice of this paradigm and provide a sample rule along with its reasoning process.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 106,
   "TYPE": "lq",
   "key": 9386
  }
 ]
}